{quote}_Our current approach towards restaurants outside parity is that the pricing is at the sole discretion of our partners but we make recommendations that prices should be aligned and in such cases, we do not invest in discounts and, more than that, we do not offer visibility in the discount on the entire menu category._

_What are we allowed and what we do instead is using comercial tools such as limiting their in app visibility, stop investing in them and overall not encouraging such behaviour._{quote}

{quote}_Each partner is free to apply promotions but if we notice that the prices shown in our app are not i line with the prices they have in the location we will minimise their visibility - meaning that if customers search for them in the search bar or in the restaurant list they will find them with no issue and the discount will be visible. However, they won’t be seen by clients navigating in the “Discount on the whole menu“ category (which is the first category that can be seen in the Bolt Food RO app) due to the fact that we want to offer that kind of visibility to partners that have competitive prices and do not maximize their them so that they will apply a discount later only to create a fake discount._{quote}

