iOS has 7 static values for {{action}} :

* {{handled}}
** Is called when stories that were opened from floating banner were closed _and_ fully watched.
** Is called when the app receives “rate app” campaign during ride hailing active order
** Is called when the app receives any modal poll campaign in micromobility flow
** 
* {{view}}
** Is called when a view for modal campaign is constructed (not necessarily immediately when it appears on the screen)
* {{tap}}
** If the modal has action (button) without {{id}} then tapping on the button will send this event.
* {{dismiss}}
** Is called when the modal campaign view is explicitly closed ([i.e|http://i.ee] by swiping it down or tapping close button). This action is not called when modal campaign view is closed by tapping an action (i.e confirmation) button.
* {{add_card_displayed}}
** Is called when “Add credit card” view is opened if it was initialized with {{modalPollingId}}
* {{add_card_button_pressed}}
** Defined, but not used
* {{add_card_added_successfully}}
** Is called when credit card was added on “Add credit card” view and the view was initialized with {{modalPollingId}}



And there’s one possible dynamic value:

*  If the modal has action (button) with {{id}} field defined, then tapping on the button will send action that is equal to the value of this {{id}} field. If the action (button) has no {{id}} defined then {{tap}} is sent intead.

