Hey [~accountid:641d5e830e6828ab20269e6d] 

I note that the Rider wants to make a Personal Injury Claim. If this is the case, the claim needs to be made against the Driver and not Bolt (Bolt is not the appropriate defendant). 

This is a generic response we send back to Riders who want to pursue personal injury claims: 

+*GENERIC RESPONSE FOR CLAIMS*+ 

{color:#ff991f}_Dear [INSERT NAME]_{color}

{color:#ff991f}_We write to you today in regards to your recent correspondence._{color}

{color:#ff991f}_We understand that you would like to make a personal injury claim, however this correspondence has been incorrectly addressed to Bolt. Please note, Bolt drivers are independent contractors and Bolt does not arrange insurance on behalf of any driver. Drivers using the Bolt platform arrange their own insurance for their vehicles._  {color}

{color:#ff991f}_In these circumstances and if you haven't done so already, you can use the registration plate of the vehicle to search for a vehicle's insurer's details at the Motor Insurance Database:_{color}[{color:#ff991f} +_https://www.askmid.com_+{color}|https://www.askmid.com/]{color:#ff991f}_._ {color}

{color:#ff991f}_From this website, you can submit a one-off search after which you will receive the policy number, name of insurers and contact details to help you progress any claim._  {color}

{color:#ff991f}_We trust that you will find this information useful._ {color}

{color:#ff991f}_Yours sincerely_ {color}

{color:#ff991f}_Bolt_ {color}

