As discussed via slack, I am reassigning you this ticket which is about the review of a lease contract for the drivers hub in Paraguay. The template was provided by the landlord. At Bolt we have a global template but it has not been translated into Spanish and adjusted to PY law. Therefore, I think it is better for us to negotiate the landlord’s contract template this time. The localisation of our template for PY is on my to-do list, but it is not a priority at the moment, as they do not rent many properties.

I am attaching our agnostic lease agreement template so that you can compare and take from it some wording if you considere it necessary.

[^Agnostic Template (1).docx]

The main provisions I would particularly look at when reviewing a lease are: 

i) duration of the agreement, 

ii) termination (I would try to include a termination for convenience clause), 

iii) subletting and assignment (I would try to include a clause so that we can sublet and/or assign the lease), 

iv) works (for example, include the possibility to carry out works with landlord consent and to remove them or be compensated by the landlord if they are retained, although this should be discussed with the business case by case), 

v) expenses.

